        "description": "Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Friday warmly welcomed Russian President Vladimir Putin, and presented him with a Russian translation of the #Thirukkural, a classical Tamil text comprising 1,330 couplets on virtue, governance and love.\n\nModi said the translation carries the timeless wisdom of the great Tamil poet-philosopher #Thiruvalluvar across languages and borders.\n\nIt was the two leaders' second meeting in less than two weeks, following their attendance at the Shanghai Cooperation Organization Summit in Bishkek from Aug. 31-Sept. 1.\n\nTheir latest meeting took place on the eve of the annual #BRICS Summit in New Delhi.",
